---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Healthcare in Andorra | SAAS and CASS"
  description="How public healthcare is organised in Andorra, from official SAAS and CASS pages: the hospital, parish primary-care centres, and social security."
  path="/healthcare"
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Healthcare</h1>
    <p>
      Public care is a small-country system: one hospital, parish
      clinics, and a social-security fund. What you are entitled to
      depends on your affiliation. Confirm that on CASS.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        Taken from
        <a href="https://saas.ad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">saas.ad</a>,
        <a href="https://www.cass.ad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cass.ad</a>
        and the
        <a
          href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/salut"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">Govern.ad health theme</a
        >. This page does not repeat reimbursement percentages or
        contribution tables. Those sit in current CASS rules and they
        change.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>SAAS, the public provider</h2>
    <p>
      The Servei Andorrà d’Atenció Sanitària is the public healthcare
      provider. On its own site it describes the
      <a
        href="https://saas.ad/unitats-assistencials/hospital-nostra-senyora-meritxell"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Hospital Nostra Senyora de Meritxell</a
      >
      as the only hospital in the Principality, in Escaldes-Engordany.
    </p>
    <p>
      SAAS also publishes a network of
      <a
        href="https://saas.ad/unitats-assistencials/atencio-primaria"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Centres d’Atenció Primària</a
      >
      (parish clinics staffed by nursing professionals, working with
      family doctors and specialists). The same pages list school health,
      mental-health services, and El Cedre, a socio-health residence.
    </p>
    <p>
      Emergency medical attention is described on the SAAS site. For a
      life-threatening emergency, use the number published there.
    </p>

    <h2>CASS, social security</h2>
    <p>
      The
      <a href="https://www.cass.ad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >Caixa Andorrana de Seguretat Social</a
      >
      is the public social-security institution. Its site covers
      affiliation, medical vouchers, and coverage when travelling to
      Spain, France or Portugal. Whether you are insured, and on what
      terms, depends on your permit, employment or other legal basis.
    </p>

    <h2>Private clinics</h2>
    <p>
      Private centres operate alongside SAAS. We list
      <a href="/directory/centre-medic-carlemany">Centre Mèdic Carlemany</a>
      because it publishes its own site. That is not an endorsement and
      it is not a substitute for CASS affiliation.
    </p>

    <p>
      Daily life context is on
      <a href="/living-in-andorra">living in Andorra</a>.
      For a permit, start with
      <a href="/become-a-resident">become a resident</a>.
      The registers themselves are on
      <a href="/official-sources">official sources</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
